hadiths[116]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will command you with two things; whichever of them you do will suffice you in place of the other, and if you are able to do both, then you know best. This (bleeding) is merely one of the kicks of Satan. So count six or seven days as menstruation according to the knowledge of Allah, then take a ritual bath (ghusl), until when you see that you have become pure and clean, pray for twenty-three or twenty-four nights and their days, and fast; this will suffice you. And do the same every month, just as women menstruate and become pure at the times of their menstruation and purity. And if you are able to delay the Zuhr and hasten the Asr, then take a ritual bath and pray both prayers, Zuhr and Asr, together; and delay the Maghrib and hasten the Isha, then take a ritual bath and pray both prayers together, then do so; and take a ritual bath with the Fajr, then do so; and fast as well if you are able. And this is the more preferable of the two to me."""
"3586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who reviles a believer is like one standing at the brink of destruction."""
"3587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two times in which the gates of heaven are opened and the supplication of one who supplicates is seldom rejected: when the prayer is established, and when ranks are formed in the way of Allah."""
"3588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who gives the people water to drink should drink last of them."""
"3589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who gives the people water to drink is the last of them to drink."""
"3590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I asked Allah for intercession for my Ummah, and He said: For you there are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment. I said: O Lord, give me more. So He scooped out (more) for me with both His hands twice, and also from His right and from His left."""
"3591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I asked Jibril: Which of the two terms did Musa (peace be upon him) fulfil? He said: The more complete and more perfect of the two (he fulfilled)."""
"3592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I asked my Lord not to punish the heedless (children) among the descendants of mankind, and He granted them to me."""
"3593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I asked my Lord for three things; He granted me two and withheld one. I asked my Lord not to destroy my Ummah by famine, and He granted it; I asked Him not to destroy my Ummah by drowning, and He granted it as well; and I asked Him not to put their hostility among themselves, and He did not grant it to me."""
"3594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Musa (peace be upon him) asked his Lord: O my Lord, who will be the lowest in rank among the people of Paradise? Allah said: He will be a man who comes after the people of Paradise have entered Paradise, and it will be said to him: Enter Paradise. He will say: O Lord, how, when the people have settled in their places and taken their shares? It will be said to him: Would you be pleased to have the like of the kingdom of one of the kings of the world? He will say: I am pleased, O Lord. Allah will say: For you is that, and as much again, and as much again, and as much again, and as much again. At the fifth time he will say: I am pleased, O Lord. Allah will say: This is for you and ten times as much besides, and for you is everything your soul desires and your eye delights in. He will say: I am pleased, O Lord. Musa (peace be upon him) asked: O Lord, then who will be the highest of them in rank? Allah said: They are the ones whom I have chosen; I planted their honour with My own hand and set a seal upon it, (such blessings) as no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and the thought of which has never crossed the heart of any human being."""
"3595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abusing a Muslim is sinfulness, and fighting him is disbelief."""
"3596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abusing a Muslim is sinfulness, fighting him is disbelief, and the sanctity of his wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."""
"3597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah)! You do not have the strength for it, nor can you bear it. Did you not say (this supplication): 'Allahumma atina fi al-dunya hasanatan wa fi al-akhirati hasanatan wa qina 'adhab al-nar' (O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire)?"""
"3598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah)! What an evil reward she gave it! She vowed to Allah that if Allah saved her on it (the she-camel), she would slaughter it, (whereas) no vow is fulfilled in disobedience to Allah, nor in something that the servant does not own."""
"3599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah)! What trials have been sent down tonight? And what treasures have been opened? Wake the women of the apartments, for many a woman who is clothed in this world will be naked in the Hereafter."""
"3600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah)! What severity has been sent down regarding debt! By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, then killed, while he owed a debt, he would not enter Paradise until his debt was paid off on his behalf."""
"3601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah)! This is just as the people of Musa (peace be upon him) said: Make for us a god just as they have gods. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, you will certainly follow the ways of those who came before you."""
"3602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are seven deeds whose reward keeps reaching the servant in his grave after his death: whoever taught knowledge, or made a stream flow, or dug a well, or planted a date palm, or built a mosque, or left a copy of the Qur'an as inheritance, or left behind a child who seeks forgiveness for him after his death."""
"3603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seven people Allah will shade in His shade on the Day when there is no shade but His: a just ruler; a young man who grew up in the worship of Allah; a man whose heart is attached to the mosque, so that when he leaves it (his heart) remains attached until he returns to it; two men who love each other for the sake of Allah, meeting on that and parting on that; a man who remembers Allah in solitude and his eyes overflow with tears; a man who is called (to sin) by a woman of status and beauty, and he says: I fear Allah, the Lord of the worlds; and a man who gives charity and conceals it so much that his left hand does not know what his right hand has spent."""
"3604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning: they are those who do not have themselves cauterised, nor cauterise others, nor seek (non-Shari'ah) incantations (ruqyah), nor take bad omens, and they put their trust in their Lord."""
"3605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prescribed term has reached its end; propose marriage to her, (addressing) her herself."""
"3606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One dirham has surpassed a hundred thousand dirhams: a man who has two dirhams takes one of them and gives it in charity, and another man who has much wealth takes a hundred thousand from his wealth and gives it in charity."""
"3607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The orphans of Badr have surpassed you (in receiving charity), but I will direct you to something better for you than that: after every prayer say Allahu Akbar thirty-three times, say Subhan Allah thirty-three times, say Alhamdulillah thirty-three times, and (then say): 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is none worthy of worship except Allah alone, He has no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things)."""
"3608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the signs of the Hour are six (things): my death; the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis; a man being given a thousand dinars and considering it insufficient; a trial whose heat will enter the home of every Muslim; a death that will spread among the people like the plague of sheep; and the Romans breaking their covenant, then they will march with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand (soldiers)."""
"3609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Day of Resurrection, a fire will come out of Hadramawt that will drive the people (to the place of gathering)."""
"3610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The screen between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the children of Adam is that when one of them takes off his garment, he says: 'Bismillah' (In the name of Allah)."""
"3611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The screen between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the children of Adam is that when one of them enters the toilet, he says: 'Bismillah' (In the name of Allah)."""
"3612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will make a secure peace with the Romans, then you and they will fight an enemy behind them, and you will be safe and take spoils. Then you will camp in a meadow with hills, and a man from the Romans will stand, raise the cross and say: The cross has prevailed! Then a man from the Muslims will rise up to him and kill him. Then the people will break the covenant and there will be great bloody battles; they will gather against you and come at you under eighty banners, under each banner ten thousand (soldiers)."""
"3613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Many lands will be conquered for you and Allah will suffice you, so let none of you neglect playing with his arrows (practising archery)."""
"3614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world will be opened up for you until you adorn your houses just as the Ka'bah is adorned, so you today are better than (you will be) on that day."""
"3615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be rulers (imams) who will speak and their words will not be rejected; (but) they will plunge into the Fire one after another just as monkeys plunge one after another."""
"3616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be new events, trial, division and disagreement; so if you are able to be the one killed and not the killer, then do so."""
"3617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be rulers whom (worldly) matters will keep busy, and they will delay the prayer from its time; so make your prayer with them voluntary."""
"3618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be rulers, and you will approve (some of their deeds) and disapprove (others). So whoever disliked (it in his heart) is free (of blame), and whoever objected (openly) is safe; but whoever was pleased and followed is not free (of blame)."""
"3619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be imams who delay the prayer from its times. Pray it on time, and then if you are present with them at the prayer, pray (with them as well)."""
"3620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be favouritism (preferring one's own) and matters you will disapprove of."" The Companions asked: Then what do you command us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfil the right (that is due) upon you, and ask Allah for (the right that is) yours."""
"3621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be many evils; so whoever you see separating from the community (jama'ah) or trying to divide the affair of the Ummah of Muhammad, whoever he may be, kill him, for the Hand of Allah is with the community, and Satan runs alongside the one who separates from the community."""
"3622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be many, many evils; so whoever wants to divide the affair of the Muslims while they are united, strike him with the sword, whoever he may be."""
"3623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be a trial in which the one sitting will be better than the one standing, the one standing will be better than the one walking, and the one walking will be better than the one running."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if someone enters my house and stretches out his hand to kill me? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be like the (righteous) son of Adam."""
"3624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be trials in which the one sitting will be better than the one standing, the one standing will be better than the one walking, and the one walking will be better than the one running. Whoever looks towards it, it will destroy him; and whoever finds in it a refuge or shelter, let him seek refuge in it."""
"3625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be mines around which the worst of people will gather."""
"3626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajdat al-sahw) in the prayer suffice (to make up) for every kind of addition and omission."""
"3627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep to moderation and try to come close (to perfection)."""
"3628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep to moderation and try to come close (to perfection), and rejoice, and know that the deeds of none of you will admit him into Paradise, nor me, unless Allah covers me with forgiveness and mercy."""
"3629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The happiness of the son of Adam is in three things, and his misery is also in three things. Of the happiness of the son of Adam are: a righteous wife, a good mount and a spacious home. And the misery of the son of Adam is in three things: a bad home, a bad wife and a bad mount."""
"3630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Her (the virgin's) silence is her consent."""
"3631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter."""
"3632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah for pardon and well-being, for no one has been given, after certainty (faith), anything better than well-being."""
"3633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah to conceal your faults and to turn your fears into safety."""
"3634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah (when supplicating) with the palms of your hands, and do not ask Him with the backs of them."""
"3635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."""
"3636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, which is the highest rank in Paradise; only one man will attain it, and I hope that I will be he."""
"3637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, for no servant in this world asks for it for me except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"3638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you heard of a city, one side of which is on land and one side in the sea? The Hour will not be established until seventy thousand of the children of Ishaq attack it. When they reach it, they will camp there; they will not fight with any weapon nor shoot a single arrow, but will say: 'La ilaha illallahu wallahu akbar' (There is none worthy of worship except Allah, and Allah is the Greatest), and one of its sides, the one in the sea, will fall. Then they will say a second time: 'La ilaha illallahu wallahu akbar', and its other side will also fall. Then they will say a third time: 'La ilaha illallahu wallahu akbar', and the way will be opened for them, and they will enter it and take spoils. Then while they are dividing the spoils, suddenly a caller will come and say: The Dajjal has emerged! So they will leave everything and return."""
"3639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name your son Abdur-Rahman."""
"3640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mention the name of Allah over it and eat it."""
"3641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name (your children) with my name, but do not take my kunyah (Abu al-Qasim)."""
"3642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name (your children) with my name, but do not take my kunyah, for I have only been sent as a distributor (qasim) who distributes (things) among you."""
"3643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surah Tabarak (al-Mulk) is the one that protects from the punishment of the grave."""
"3644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A surah of the Qur'an consisting of only thirty verses argued on behalf of its reciter (before Allah) until it admitted him into Paradise, and it is Surah Tabarak."""
"3645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you bury the dead, keep the graves level with the ground (flat)."""
"3646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows, or else Allah will cause discord between your faces (hearts)."""
"3647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of establishing the prayer."""
"3648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows, so that discord does not enter your hearts."""
"3649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In a time of tribulation, a man's safety lies in staying in his house."""
"3650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Deceptive years will come upon the people, in which the liar will be regarded as truthful and the truthful as a liar, the treacherous will be regarded as trustworthy and the trustworthy as treacherous, and in them the Ruwaybidah will speak. It was asked: What is the Ruwaybidah? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The contemptible, worthless man who speaks about the affairs of the public."""
"3651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will come to you seeking knowledge. When you see them, say to them: Welcome, in accordance with the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and give them (religious) guidance."""
"3652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sayhan, Jayhan, the Euphrates and the Nile are all among the rivers of Paradise."""
"3653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will emerge from my Ummah who will drink the Qur'an (recite it) just as they drink milk."""
"3654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times, people will emerge who are young in age and foolish in mind. They will speak the best words of creation. They will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game. So when you meet them, kill them, for in killing them there is a reward with Allah on the Day of Resurrection for the one who kills them."""
"3655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep moving, this is Jumdan (a mountain). The Mufarridun have gone ahead: those men who remember Allah much and those women who remember Allah."""
"3656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This religion will also be strengthened by men who will have no share with Allah."""
"3657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When they become Muslims, they will both give charity and wage jihad."""
"3658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Ummah will be afflicted by the same disease that afflicted the (earlier) nations: arrogance, insolence, the race for abundance of wealth in the world, mutual rancour, hatred and envy, until transgression and oppression arise."""
"3659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The matter will reach the point where you become organised armies: an army in Syria (al-Sham), an army in Yemen and an army in Iraq. Hold fast to Syria, for it is the chosen land of Allah, to which He draws His chosen servants. If you refuse that, then hold fast to your Yemen and keep drawing water from your pools, for Allah has taken it upon Himself, for my sake, to look after Syria and its people."""
"3660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game."""
"3661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be rulers of whom you will approve (some deeds) and disapprove (others). Whoever openly opposes them will be saved, whoever keeps away from them will remain safe, and whoever mingles with them will be ruined."""
"3662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me there will be people from my Ummah who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game, and then they will not return to it. They will be the worst of all creation. Their sign will be the shaving of the head."""
"3663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be men in my Ummah who will eat all kinds of food, drink all kinds of drinks, wear all kinds of clothes and speak with affectation and pretension. These will be the worst people of my Ummah."""
"3664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rulers will be placed over you who will delay the prayer beyond its times and introduce innovations. Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: Then what should I do? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O son of Umm Abd! You ask me what you should do? There is no obedience to the one who disobeys Allah."""
"3665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times there will be the swallowing up by the earth, a rain of stones and the transformation of forms, when musical instruments and singing girls become widespread and wine is regarded as lawful."""
"3666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times there will be police officers (government agents) who will go out in the morning in the wrath of Allah and return in the evening in the displeasure of Allah."""
"3667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last times there will be people from my Ummah who will tell you things that neither you nor your forefathers have heard. So beware of them."""
"3668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be disagreement and division in my Ummah. There will be people who speak fine words but do evil deeds. They will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game. They will not return (to the religion) until the arrow returns to its notch. They will be the worst of all creation. Glad tidings for the one who kills them and the one whom they kill. They will call to the Book of Allah, yet they will have nothing to do with it. Whoever fights them will be closer to Allah than they are. Their sign will be the shaving of the head."""
"3669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be people in my Ummah who will deny divine decree (al-qadar)."""
"3670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be people who will eat by means of their tongues (through flattery), just as a cow grazes from the earth."""
"3671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be people who will transgress the limits in supplication."""
"3672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me, your affairs will be taken over by men who will present to you as good the things you consider evil, and present as evil the things you consider good. So whoever among you lives to see that, there is no obedience to the one who disobeys Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"3673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Muslims will light fires with the bows, arrows and shields of Gog and Magog (Ya'juj and Ma'juj) for seven years."""
"3674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best form of seeking forgiveness is that you say: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no true god except You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as far as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your blessing upon me, and I also acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. Whoever says it during the day with full conviction and dies on that day before the evening, he is among the people of Paradise; and whoever says it at night with full conviction and dies before the morning, he is among the people of Paradise."""
"3675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The leader of the martyrs is Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib, and a man who stands before an unjust ruler and commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and he (the ruler) kills him."""
"3676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The leader of the martyrs with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib."""
"3677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the fragrant plants of the people of Paradise is henna."""
"3678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The leading women of the people of Paradise are four: Maryam, Fatimah, Khadijah and Asiyah."""
"3679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The grazing animal (the compensation for damage it causes) is waived, the well (if harm occurs by falling into it, that) is waived, the mine (if an accident occurs in it, that) is waived, and on buried treasure there is one-fifth (as zakah)."""
"3680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who strives on behalf of the widow and the needy is like the one who wages jihad in the path of Allah, or like the one who stands in prayer at night and fasts by day."""
"3681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Seven Oft-Repeated (al-Sab' al-Mathani) is Surah al-Fatihah."""
"3682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prostration in Surah Sad was performed by Dawud (peace be upon him) as repentance, and we perform it in gratitude."""
"3683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eating the pre-dawn meal (suhur) is a blessing, so do not abandon it, even if one of you only takes a single sip of water, for Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who eat the pre-dawn meal."""
"3684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper (izar) may wear trousers, and whoever cannot find sandals may wear leather socks (khuffs)."""
"3685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fortunate one is he whose good fortune was written while he was still in his mother's womb, and the wretched one is he whose wretchedness was written while he was still in his mother's womb."""
"3686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Travel is a piece of torment; it keeps one of you from his food, his drink and his sleep. So when one of you has fulfilled his need, let him hasten back to his family."""
"3687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lower part is easier (more convenient)."""
"3688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Proceed calmly, O servants of Allah! Proceed calmly."""
"3689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tranquillity and calm are found among the owners of sheep and goats."""
"3690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Credit (dealing) until the birth of the unborn young in the she-camel's womb is usury (riba)."""
"3691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tuberculosis (dying of consumption) is martyrdom."""
"3692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A good demeanour, deliberateness and moderation are one part of the twenty-four parts of prophethood."""
"3693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listening and obeying is obligatory upon the Muslim man, whether he likes it or dislikes it, as long as he is not commanded to commit disobedience. If he is commanded to commit disobedience, then there is no listening and no obedience."""
"3694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The cat is one of the household, and it is among those (pure) animals that go about around you."""
"3695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The miswak is a means of purification for the mouth and of the pleasure of the Lord."""
"3696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The miswak makes the mouth fragrant and pleases the Lord."""
"3697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As-Salam is one of the names of Allah which Allah has placed on earth, so spread it among yourselves. For when a Muslim man passes by a people and greets them with salam, and they return his greeting, he gains a degree of superiority over them because he reminded them of the salam. And if they do not return his greeting, one who is better and purer than them (an angel) returns it to him."""
"3698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Peace be upon you, O abode of believing people! And we, if Allah wills, will be joining you. I wish that we had seen our brothers."" The Companions asked: ""Are we not your brothers?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No, rather you are my companions. Our brothers are those who have not yet come."" The Companions asked: ""How will you recognise those of your Ummah who have not yet come?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What do you think, if a man had horses with white blazes on their foreheads and white legs among a herd of pure black horses, would he not recognise his horses?"" The Companions said: ""Of course!"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then they (my Ummah) will come on the Day of Resurrection with faces, hands and feet shining from the traces of ablution, and I will have gone ahead of them to the Pond. Beware! Some men will be driven away from my Pond just as a stray camel is driven away. I will call out to them: 'Come here! Come here!' Then it will be said: 'They changed (the religion) after you.' So I will say: 'Away with them, away with them, away with them!'"""
"3699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greeting of salam comes before speaking. So whoever starts talking to you before greeting you with salam, do not answer him."""
"3700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Sayyid (the true Master) is Allah."""
